BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
CASE NO: Crl.R.C.\(MD\) No. 340 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD011123452026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi

PARTIES:
Selvi and Minor Daughter Kaviya
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
K. Rajendran \(Husband\)
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
CrPC Section 125, BNSS Section 144, CrPC Section 397

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Maintenance, Section 125 CrPC, Standard of Living, Income Tax Returns, Financial Capacity

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Husband, earning Rs. 1.2 Lakhs as government school headmaster, neglected wife and daughter. Trial court granted meager Rs. 6,000.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
What is the quantum benchmark for maintenance under Section 125 CrPC / 144 BNSS relative to husband's net salary?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Wife and children are entitled to live with identical socioeconomic dignity and comfort enjoyed in the matrimonial household.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Criminal Revision Allowed; Maintenance enhanced from Rs. 6,000 to Rs. 22,000 per month reflecting husband's IT returns.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
